   "line": [
    "c4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The pawn to c4 is the Maróczy Bind — White grips d5 and e4 and plays for a slow squeeze. At club level it is far less scary than its reputation: it demands very precise positional play from White, and Black has a string of tricky responses.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "The Maróczy Bind is a positional clamp, not an attack — it punishes imprecise handling, not the defender.",
   "plans": "Trade a pair of knights, keep the c6-pawn as a clamp of your own, and press the semi-open b-file."
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 2903.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppp1p/2n2np1/8/2PNP3/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
