   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/p2ppp1p/2p2np1/4P3/2P5/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And the follow-up e5 walks into it — a very tempting pawn thrust that simply loses.",
   "kind": "trap",
   "teaches": "A tempting central push can hang to an in-between check — always look for the zwischenzug first.",
   "plans": "Answer with the queen check on a5."
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 2918,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/p2ppp1p/2p2np1/q3P3/2P5/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Qa5+"
   ],
   "spoken": "The point: the queen check on a5 wins the e5-pawn back with interest — never forget this resource. After the block, the pawn falls and Black is a healthy pawn up.",
   "kind": "trap",
   "teaches": "The queen check on a5 is the standard refutation of White's e5 grab in this line.",
   "plans": "Collect e5, then finish developing a clean pawn up."
